  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5bb28bc074284837af91712bbd7fd25f",
      "statement": "Cutting a myfeeder release requires this exact order: `./gradlew release` (axion cut+push tag) before `./gradlew clean bootJar`, otherwise the jar is stamped as a -SNAPSHOT version; `$VERSION` must then be read via `./gradlew currentVersion -q` piped through `grep 'Project version'` to strip terminal control sequences.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://build.gradle.kts#L75-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8465135d799683f416cfd387d16ed2fc3b0a8138d8f9c8ef1b029861daf77870:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy.sh#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72ad51672eb364ab3bca9727e6c4fb5c6448ffc152463dd83893d9c0f527a0ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2afa0ba28ad64092bab81f7790fc2b75",
      "statement": "deploy.sh performs `helm upgrade --install` against the `myfeeder` chart/namespace, requires MYFEEDER_PG_PASSWORD and MYFEEDER_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (script uses `set -u` so these are mandatory), and treats MYFEEDER_RAINDROP_API_TOKEN as optional, defaulting to empty and printing a warning if unset.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy.sh",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:17de04c3fcc740d7d4b19cb28fa0918f08a0290262ddddc39b918270866e4573"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d6d711a32c04ce58ead0497f6c80695",
      "statement": "The runtime image is built from a hand-written Dockerfile (eclipse-temurin:25-jre) rather than Spring Boot's bootBuildImage/Paketo buildpacks, specifically to avoid a Docker 29 containerd image-store bug that corrupts buildpack image exports and causes k3s pods to fail with a wrong-diffID error on pull.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:134757ee431d37409bebc354602e1d8b9180dd485373ae6e41051a4b51bc03ec:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://build.gradle.kts#L128-L133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b28a42d5c4733d9f61fded2992abbb5f70e8405e22975ff9a4b2d067242c3543:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d708054fc4f4e399f525f9782d76bd5",
      "statement": "The Dockerfile only COPYs build/libs/*.jar, so the frontend must already be embedded in that jar; `./gradlew clean bootJar` chains npmBuild → processResources so `clean` forces a fresh SPA embed, and the `jar` task is disabled to keep the `build/libs/*.jar` glob unambiguous (no -plain jar).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L1-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e0a14b7f2fbf14ec5d4b603c12be40e651e00bdd9e4c57cae64ba1be33d3d88:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://build.gradle.kts#L108-L133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3da5c6809b213127a4753402a5cecf0a0268364e30d7baa525c55b5497a77b1b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_35113f22fa0f420ea598a50de54219bb",
      "statement": "The Helm chart (helm/myfeeder) deploys only the app Deployment/Service and an in-cluster Redis; PostgreSQL is not templated in the chart and is instead reached as an external service at pg.bartram.org via the externalPostgres values, injected into SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL by the app ConfigMap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://helm/myfeeder/templates/app-configmap.yaml",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:f7ce878c344977f85329117727367c8860f194122c2ae9334e20cde3851fe40e"
